**定理 81.1（joint actual-source law）。** Fix the genuine neutral-free plateau parameters L>1, 1<d0<L^(2/phi^2), H=1 and a fixed E0<1/2. Choose the least integer $K\geq1$ with $2^{-K}\leq\min(E,1/2)$, so $K=O(1+\log(1/E))$. Put $c_0=1-1/d_0>0$. From §77, $D\geq c_0/N$; a largest-dyadic-below-$D$ choice, or the acquired bin, has $2^{-h}\geq D/4$, hence $h\leq\max(0,\lceil\log_2(4N/c_0)\rceil)$. The gamma length in §76 therefore gives the upper bound, uniformly for $0<E\leq E_0$,

$$C_N(E)\leq C\left[1+\log(1/E)+\log\log(N+2)\right].$$

for all sufficiently large N, with C depending only on the fixed parameters and E0. This is a numerical COMPLETE word under the specified evidence convention; the universal interpreter and all its source-dependent fields are included. No fixed N is installed in the decoder.

Here is the simpler actual constant-Delta family for the lower. Choose a fixed real s with sqrt(d0)<s<L^(1/phi^2), z=log s>0. Let k be a sufficiently large positive multiple of six, m=F_k, n=F_(k+1), and t_k=rho^(k+1)(alpha), with F_(k+2) leaves. Use the ONE preparation (s^(1+n/m)e1, s^(-n/m)e2). Its determinant is s^2, its beta length is <1, and its alpha length tends to s^(phi^2)<L. The ordered-source parity/period is the same at all these k. Cassini gives Q=m^2+mn-n^2=-1; direct orthogonal homogeneity gives q0=q2=exp(-z/m), q1=1. Thus every original read bound is satisfied and q_j=exp(-(z/m)F_(j-1)). This is an actual source and preparation, not a scalar process pasted into the goal.

Give an E0-uniform packing. Set g=1-2E0>0 and a=g/8. Choose an integer q>=1 with 13^q*a>=log(4/g). Consecutive allowed indices spaced 6q apart have rate ratio at least 13^q, since F_(k+6)>=13F_k. Increase k_min so lambda=z/F_k<a for all indices used. For any two distinct rates lambda_slow<lambda_fast, choose the first j>=3 with lambda_slow F_(j-1)>=a; the Fibonacci one-step ratio is at most two, so its exponent lies in [a,2a]. The slow amplitude is >=exp(-2a)>=1-2a=2E0+3g/4; the fast amplitude is <=exp(-13^q a)<=g/4. Identical phase directions give trajectory distance at least 2E0+g/2>2E0. There are at least c log(N+2) such legal trees of size <=N for all sufficiently large N. Their words must be distinct for every E<=E0, yielding a lower c1 loglog(N+2)-C1 with constants uniform in E.

A separate actual sphere packing supplies the precision term in the SAME domain. Fix one sufficiently late member with first-future amplitude r_*=exp(-z/F_k)>max(E0,1/2). Rotate its entire single preparation by SO(3), preserving determinant, tree and every read bound. Its x3 ranges over the sphere of radius r_*. A maximal set with pairwise distances >2E covers the sphere by closed caps of chordal radius 2E, each of area at most 4pi E^2; hence it has at least r_*^2/E^2 members when E<r_*/2. Each needs a different word. The antipodal pair also supplies a positive baseline for E in the remaining compact range up to E0. Thus there is a lower c2[1+log(1/E)]. The maximum of these two lower bounds is at least a fixed positive multiple of their sum after increasing the common N_min and adjusting constants. Therefore

$$C_N(E)=\Theta_{L,d_0,E_0}\!\left(1+\log(1/E)+\log\log(N+2)\right),\quad 0<E\leq E_0<\tfrac12,\quad N\geq N_{\min}.$$

The scale and sphere packings are both actual legal sources; E0-uniformity is established without taking an E-dependent scale separation. A fixed-E statement is a weaker corollary, not a separate discovery. This does not extend to E=1/2 via a non-strict packing inequality.

There is a distinct exact-rational refinement. Choose a positive rational c strictly between log(sqrt d0) and log(L)/phi^2. For the same k,m,n put b_k=1+c/m and prepare (b_k^(m+n)e1,b_k^(-n)e2). These are finite exact rationals. Delta=b_k^(2m) tends to exp(2c)>d0; the alpha length tends to exp(c phi^2)<L; q0=q2=b_k^-1, q1=1, and the directions are unchanged. The rates log(1+c/m) lie between c/(m+c) and c/m, giving a ratio at least 13/2 for consecutive k spaced six once m>=c. Replacing 13 by 13/2 in the preceding fixed separation proves the SAME joint lower within this rational restricted class; rotate by rational SO(3) matrices (dense rational quaternion rotations) for a finite sphere packing, reducing the chordal slack before selecting rational approximants. Exact source presentation can cost O(N log(N+2)) bits even though the retained numerical word costs loglog N. This refinement adds rational-interface scope; the constant-Delta family remains the simpler unrestricted proof. Scaled-critical families are equivalent sharp-order witnesses and are not accumulated as extra novelty.

